  "v": "0.1",
  "about": "Word forms the node reads in a time slot (en, de, gsw incl. Bernese, Basel and Zurich forms) and resolves to an absolute time in the node's time zone. A time is either relative ('in' + a duration from duration-lexicon.json) or a set of parts: a day or weekday, a part of the day, and a clock time ('am füfi', 'halbi nüni' = 8:30, 'viertel ab drü' = 3:15, '14:30'). A weekday may be joined with a part of the day ('Mäntigmorge'). Anything else is refused. Every form is lowercase and belongs to exactly one entry.",
